---
description: Unison Brain persistent memory tools — use them proactively
alwaysApply: true
---

You have access to Unison Brain MCP tools for persistent memory across coding sessions:

- `unison_search`: Search before answering questions about previous work, bugs, decisions, or patterns
- `unison_write`: Save decisions, fixes, preferences when user asks or when clearly valuable
- `unison_get`: Read a specific document by path
- `unison_list`: List recent notes and documents
- `unison_edit`: Surgically update an existing document
- `unison_delete`: Remove a document
- `unison_tag`: Add or remove tags on a document
- `unison_resolve_entity`: Find a person, project, or concept in the knowledge graph
- `unison_facts_about`: Get known facts about an entity
- `unison_record_fact`: Record a new fact about an entity
- `unison_neighbors`: Explore related documents
- `unison_grep`: Find exact strings or patterns across document bodies
- `unison_namespaces`: Show available path namespaces (/private/, /tenant/, /teams/<slug>/)
- `unison_status`: Check brain health and document counts
- `unison_whoami`: Show current auth identity

When to use:
- User mentions past sessions, previous work, or "last time" → search first
- User says "remember", "save this", "don't forget" → write immediately
- After solving a hard bug → save the solution and root cause
- Discovering architectural patterns or conventions → save them
- User asks why something was done a certain way → search for context
- User mentions a person by name → resolve entity first

Scope: use /private/notes/ for personal notes, /tenant/ for team-shared knowledge.
